---
import ServiceSection from "../components/ServiceSection.astro";
import Endpoint from "../components/Endpoint.astro";
import RustSchema from "../components/RustSchema.astro";
---

<ServiceSection id="service-profile">
  <Fragment slot="title"><code>Prfl</code> — profile data</Fragment>
<p>This document labels slot 14 as <code>Prfl</code>. Embedded type names use the
    <code>Profile</code> namespace.</p>
    <p class="endpoint-index">
      <a href="#profile-read">Prfl/0 Read</a><a href="#profile-address-query">Prfl/1 AddressQuery</a>
      <a href="#profile-resolve-handle">Prfl/2 ResolveToonHandleToName</a>
      <a href="#profile-resolve-toon">Prfl/3 ResolveToonNameToHandle</a><a href="#profile-settings-available">Prfl/4 SettingsAvailable</a>
      <a href="#profile-change-settings">Prfl/5 ChangeSettings</a><a href="#profile-stats-event">Prfl/8 SendStatsUIEvent</a>
    </p>

    <Endpoint id="profile-read" direction="bidirectional" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Prfl/0</code> Profile::Read</Fragment>
      <p>Reads a field path from a profile record. To read a roster avatar, use the
      profile address from presence. Use path <code>04</code>. This path selects
      <code>ToonProfile.m_avatar</code>.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`// client → server
struct ReadRequest {
    client_hash: u32,
    request_id: u32,
    record_address: RecordAddress,
    specification: FullReadSpecification,
}

struct FullReadSpecification {
    selection: ReadSelection,
    reader: Option<ReaderList>,
}

enum ReadSelection {
    All { prefix_path: Vec<u8> },
    Slice {
        prefix_path: Vec<u8>,
        slice_start: Option<i64>,
        slice_end: Option<i64>,
        row_limit: Option<u32>,
        single_depth: Option<bool>,
    },
    Random,
    MultiPath { paths: Vec<Vec<u8>> },
    Range,
    HeroStats,
}

// server → client
struct ReadResponse {
    result: ReadResult,
    request_id: u32,
}

enum ReadResult {
    Start(ReadStart),
    Block(ReadBlock),
    Failure(ReadFailure),
    Cache(ReadCache),
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">Both directions differ from reflection member
      order. A returned avatar is an <code>ImageTableEntry</code> containing the
      retail <code>ICON</code> atlas ID and row-major cell offset. Captured
      selection forms include <code>All</code>, <code>Slice</code>, and
      <code>MultiPath</code>. Generated request code places one reserved bit
      before the three-bit selection and the optional-reader presence bit before
      the selected payload.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="profile-resolve-handle" direction="bidirectional" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="request capture decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Prfl/2</code> Profile::ResolveToonHandleToName</Fragment>
      <p>Looks up display names for up to 32 toon handles in one request.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`// client → server
record ResolveToonHandleToNameRequest {
    operation: ResolveToonHandleToName,
    handles: Array<ToonHandle> {
        count_bits: 6,
        count_range: 0..=32,
    },
}

record ResolveToonHandleToName {}

// server → client
record ResolveToonHandleToNameResponse {
    operation: ResolveToonHandleToName,
    responses: Array<HandleToNameResponse> {
        count_bits: 6,
        count_range: 0..=32,
    },
}

record HandleToNameResponse {
    result: u16,
    handle: ToonHandle,
    name: Option<ToonFullName>,
    tag: Option<String>,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">The operation field occupies zero bits. The
      captured request uses metadata member order and contains one handle.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="profile-change-settings" direction="client → server" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="capture decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Prfl/5</code> Profile::ChangeSettings</Fragment>
      <p>Writes indexed string settings for the account, game account, or active
      toon.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct ChangeSettings {
    string_settings: Vec<StringSetting>, // count: 7 wire bits, maximum 100
    setting_type: SettingType,
}

struct StringSetting {
    wire_tag: Bits<29>,
    value: String, // byte count: 10 wire bits; then byte-align
    index: u32,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">A capture includes the setting
      <code>BattleAuthentication.AccountCountry</code>. The 29-bit per-entry tag is
      generated wire state preceding the logical string value.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="profile-stats-event" direction="client → server" phase="protected" structure="verified reflected order" status="capture decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Prfl/8</code> Profile::SendStatsUIEvent</Fragment>
      <p>Sends an opaque event block generated by the SC2 interface.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct SendStatsUIEvent {
    events: Vec<u8>,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="profile-address-query" direction="bidirectional" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Prfl/1</code> Profile::AddressQuery</Fragment>
      <p>Resolves a Battle.net account ID to a profile record address. Use the
      result with <code>Prfl/0</code>.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`// client → server
struct AddressQueryRequest {
    request_id: u32,
    player_target: PlayerTarget,
}

enum PlayerTarget { AccountId(u32) }

// server → client
struct AddressQueryResponse {
    request_id: u32,
    result: Option<AddressQueryResult>,
}

enum AddressQueryResult {
    Success { address: RecordAddress },
    Failure { error: u32 },
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="profile-resolve-toon" direction="bidirectional" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Prfl/3</code> Profile::ResolveToonNameToHandle</Fragment>
      <p>Resolves a <code>ToonName</code> to a complete <code>ToonHandle</code>. Use
      the handle to select a whisper target.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`// client → server
struct ResolveToonNameRequest {
    name: ToonFullName,
}

// server → client
struct ResolveToonNameResponse {
    name: ToonFullName,
    result: u16,
    handle: ToonHandle,
}

struct ToonFullName {
    region: u8,
    program_id: FourCC,
    realm: u32,
    name: String,
}

struct ToonHandle {
    region: u8,
    program_id: FourCC,
    realm: u32,
    id: u64,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="profile-settings-available" direction="server → client" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Prfl/4</code> Profile::SettingsAvailable</Fragment>
      <p>Announces a profile settings record. Address the record by type, field
      path, and record address.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct SettingsAvailable {
    setting_type: SettingType,
    path: Vec<u8>, // 0..=32 bytes
    address: RecordAddress,
}

enum SettingType { Account = 1, Game = 2, Toon = 3 }

struct RecordAddress {
    label: u32,
    id: u64,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">Reflection lists address before path. The generated
      client reads type, path, then address.</p>
    </Endpoint>
</ServiceSection>
